On Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:43:34 -0700, Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com> wrote:
>> pull new messages, so nothing an agent does here can flag, move, or
>> delete mail on Fastmail, and the local copy only ever grows.
>
> We describe it as append-only - how did only ever grows get in here?

My mistake. You asked for "append-only" in the v3 review, and I fixed
it in spec.org but wrote the 4/6 commit message fresh without
checking it against the spec. v9 says "the local maildir is
append-only", the spec's words.

>> +UserCmd "sed 's/ .*//' /data/secrets/mail-creds"
>> +PassCmd "sed 's/^[^ ]* //' /data/secrets/mail-creds"
>
> This is ugly, use cut or awk.

v9 uses cut:

    UserCmd "cut -d' ' -f1 /data/secrets/mail-creds"
    PassCmd "cut -d' ' -f2- /data/secrets/mail-creds"

-f2- keeps the rest of the line, so a password with a space survives,
as the spec requires. awk '{print $2}' would cut it at the space.

> Same as cmment from previous commit. Data dirs should be created by
> operator before launching the jail.

Agreed; the maildir and mbsync dirs move to the operator's setup
block in the README, as I answered on 2/6.
